<p>To start the afternoon, head to <strong>Place Rossetti, in the heart of Vieux-Nice,</strong> to visit the magnificent, baroque <strong>cathedral of Sainte-Raparate,</strong> not forgetting to treat yourself to a delicious home-made ice-cream in one of the many stalls adjoining the square. Lose yourself in the narrow streets of Vieux-Nice until you find <strong>Place Garibaldi</strong> and its superb trompe l&#8217;oeil. You can then reach <strong>the</strong> <strong>Place Masséna</strong> by strolling along <strong>the Promenade du Paillon</strong>, the city&#8217;s green lung. In the square, admire the perfect harmony between the pastel-coloured façades and the modernism of <em>Conversation</em>, the aerial work by Catalan artist Jaume Plensa. After a snack or refreshment on the terrace of one of the square&#8217;s cafés, it&#8217;s time to indulge in some <strong>shopping in the Carré d&#8217;Or boutiques</strong> or on the majestic <strong>Avenue Jean-Médecin,</strong> starting with the famous <strong>Galeries Lafayette</strong> before making your way to <strong>Nicetoile</strong>. The day can end where it began, by the sea. And why not enjoy a romantic moonlit dinner on one of the many private beaches along the Promenade des Anglais?</p>


