    </div>



<p>Then take a step back in time. Head for the elegant <strong>Cimiez district</strong>, where you&#8217;ll discover <strong>the former Hotel Regina</strong>, specially built for Queen Victoria, followed by <strong>a visit to the Monastery and its gardens</strong>. Next stop is the <strong>Nice Archaeological Museum</strong>, with a stroll through the remains of the Roman arena, before finishing the afternoon with a <strong>visit to the Matisse Museum or the Marc Chagall National Museum</strong>, both located in the district.</p>



<p>At aperitif time, climb onto one of the <strong>city&#8217;</strong>s many <strong>rooftops</strong> to admire the sunset. Why not continue the evening in one of the restaurants in the Garibaldi district, then in the festive atmosphere of rue Bonaparte and Place du Pin, the Mecca of Nice nightlife.</p>


