<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Day 3: sea air and a break in the vineyards</h2>



<p>Visiting Nice in three days means enjoying the pleasure of wandering around as you please, while soaking up its unique atmosphere, where the charm of tradition blends harmoniously with the modernism of this great metropolis. To the programme for the first two days, why not add on day 3 <strong>a sea trip on a coastal boat to Villefranche-sur-Mer</strong>. If you prefer to walk, take <strong>the sublime coastal path linking the Cap de Nice to the divine harbour of Villefranche</strong>, where the turquoise waters compete with the shimmering colours of the houses of this town with its feet in the water. On your return (on foot, by bus or by train), treat yourself to a lunch of fish or shellfish at the Port Lympia to enjoy the bustle of this ever-changing district.</p>



<p>In the afternoon, if you have a car, head off to <strong>discover a wine estate on the Bellet hill </strong>and taste one of the delicious vintages of this sun-drenched PDO. On your return to town, take advantage of the many shops and <strong>stroll through the pedestrian zone</strong>, where you can dine and enjoy the cosmopolitan atmosphere of the area.</p>


