<p>You can, of course, personalise this 3rd day to suit your own wishes.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>For more authenticity:</strong> the Libération market, the former Gare du Sud station and its listed façade await you. </li>



<li><strong>For the more sporty and nature lovers:</strong> take a walk to Cap de Nice and climb Mont Boron, where you&#8217;ll enjoy a sublime view of Nice and the harbour of Villefranche-sur-Mer.</li>



<li><strong>For culture and heritage buffs: </strong>opt for one of the guided tours offered by the Centre du Patrimoine, discover the Palais Lascaris in Vieux-Nice, climb to the top of the Tour Saint-François, or delve into the heart of Nice&#8217;s Baroque heritage. </li>



<li><strong>For families:</strong> the Phoenix Park is a must, with its lush greenhouses and numerous animals. For an even more adventurous experience, there&#8217;s a rope park for children aged 3 and over, as well as a thrill-seeking park for older children.</li>
</ul>


